| `tests.cache_max_entries` | integer | `256` in keel and in a generated project; absent, the same value, which its reader reports as `[using default] tests.cache_max_entries = 256` | a whole number, 1 or more | `tests/bounded_cache.py` (`max_entries`, read by `bounded` when it decorates), through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `tests.cache_max_entries` row | Sets the most entries one cache a test module builds with `bounded` holds; past it the least recently used entry is dropped and its call runs again, so a smaller value is slower, never wrong. The assertion-quality gate builds its parsed-module cache per scan; other consumers may build theirs at collection. A value below 1 or not an integer stops cache construction, naming this key. | a cache in `src/` or `scripts/`: ruff TID251 bans `functools.cache` and `functools.lru_cache` there too, and neither has a bounded helper yet | always |
